WEBVTT

NOTE Neighbors (1920) - Riah TV captions

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:08.490
Buster Keaton in "Neighbors"

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:11.250
Written and directed by
Buster Keaton and Eddie Cline

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:24.000
The Flower of Love could find no
more romantic spot in which to
blossom than in this poet's
Dream Garden.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:28.200
[music]

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:24.500
"Are you comfortable?"

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:02.250
"I know a better way than
that to break his neck."

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:07.000
"He's my son and I'll break
his neck any way I please."

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:57.000
"Babe Ruth is at bat."

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:59.500
That afternoon the young
inventor tries his patent
fly-swatter.

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:22.500
"Come in!"

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:48.500
They are going to have peace
even if they have to go to Court
and fight for it.

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:09.750
"Her father's abused her long
enough. Now I want to marry her
and take her home to my father."

00:11:22.750 --> 00:11:24.750
"Sign this bond to
keep the peace."

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:37.500
"We're going to get married."

00:11:56.000 --> 00:12:01.000
After going to court to end
their troubles they have a
wedding to start more.

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:29.000
"What happened to you?"

00:12:29.750 --> 00:12:31.250
"I bought a Ford."

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:41.500
"Get the groom—the
bride's out in the alley."

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:29.500
"In giving up single life I
feel I'm losing something—"

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:24.750
"Where's the ring?"

00:15:15.750 --> 00:15:19.000
Straight from Woolworths.

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:03.500
"Father's watching—come get me!"

00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:30.500
THE END
